# Yasin3D PETG — Prusa MK3S+, 0.4 / 0.6 nozzle
# Yasin3D publishes no technical data sheet, so every printing number here is
# Prusa's Generic PETG value, unmodified.
# Parent is Generic PETG, not Prusament PETG: Prusament PETG carries
# `nozzle_diameter[0]!=0.6` and would hide this profile on a 0.6 nozzle.
inherits = Generic PETG
filament_vendor = Yasin3D
filament_type = PETG
filament_diameter = 1.75
filament_cost = 39
filament_spool_weight = 1000
filament_notes = "Yasin3D PETG - no vendor data sheet exists.\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY KNOWN: the vendor, the material type, 1.75 mm, and the price. Everything else - 240 C, 85/90 C bed, 30-50 % fan, 8 mm3/s, density 1.27 - is inherited from Prusa's Generic PETG and is a generic default, not a Yasin3D figure.\n\nPRICE: 39 ILS incl. VAT, product 'PETG Yasin3D 1KG' at filamentcenter.co.il (checked 29 Aug 2026).\n\nWORTH KNOWING BEFORE THE FIRST PRINT: the inherited bed is 85 C first layer / 90 C, which is where PETG bonds to a smooth PEI sheet hard enough to pull PEI off it on removal. Either use the textured sheet, or put down a thin glue-stick release layer, or drop the bed toward 70-75 C. The Inslogic PETG Pro profiles in this repo take the last option because Inslogic's own sheet sanctions it; there is no Yasin3D sheet to sanction anything, so the parent's value is left in place here rather than invented.\n\nUNTESTED - no calibration print has been run with this profile yet."
